    69	  - The BASE arm's validity is taken as on file: arm 1 = VALID by dec 069 (ENV CONTROL caveat, plan 007 l.152, on every citation);
    70	    arm 2 = plan 008's verdict. If the base is invalid or not ruled, the arm-3 pairing goes to the Director (no rule applies).
    71	  - ENV DRIFT record (review non-blocking 5): the arm-3 results header lists docker image digest, vLLM / google-adk / swegemma
    72	    versions, model id, GPU names/count, setup and verification wall p50/p90, for arm 3 AND the base; differences are listed, not
    73	    ruled on. Wall-p90 SAFETY comparisons are cited with this list.
    74	- MAIN = ids 3..33 of the registered order, same bundle sha and kernel code as the smoke. Smoke rows count toward the 33 only if the
    75	  smoke PASSED and the shas match (as plan 007 arm 1: smoke 3 + main 30). Missing ids after main follow the D73.7 rule (plan 008
    76	  l.256-260) verbatim, with "arm 3" for "arm 2".
    77	- Sequencing: after the dec 055 31b-v002 submit, after arm 2 is complete and classified (the base depends on it), inside the weekly
    78	  quota. Quota logged before and after the smoke and the main (dec 063/064). Estimate: smoke ~0.6 h, main ~11 h (arm-1 main was
    79	  +10.41 h for 30 ids; the 3.5-min cap bounds agent time, so thinking adds at most its share of the cap). Arm 2 (~11.5 h) + arm 3
    80	  (~11.6 h) ~= 23 of 30 h. If the measured arm-2 cost leaves < 13 h, the arm-3 schedule goes back to the Director with the numbers.
    81	
    82	## Metrics (paired against the BASE arm on the same 33 ids; one script, codex-reviewed BEFORE arm-3 data exists)
    83	Implementation: an `arm3` mode in eval/plan008_metrics.py (same definitions), plus thinking counts per eval/thinking_bound.py. Built
    84	only after this plan's review is CLEAN. Inputs (review non-blocking 6): arm-3 rows = smoke + main + any chunk dirs aggregated to
    85	exactly 33 unique ids (first attempts retained, D73.7 duplicate precedence, exit non-zero otherwise); base rows = the base arm's
    86	existing dirs (arm 1: smoke 3 + main 30; arm 2: its run dir(s)), same aggregation rule.
    87	- PRIMARY: resolved discordant pairs ON-only (arm 3 resolved, base not) / OFF-only, exact two-sided sign test; governing classifier,
    88	  same resolved rule as the arm-1 primary. Also arm-3 resolved/33 with a Wilson 95% CI.
    89	- TIMING (plan 007 cap-3.5 check, verbatim): every arm-3 row has non-null agent_clock_seconds <= 220 s and finalization_seconds <= 30 s.
    90	- TIMEOUTS: arm-3 timeouts vs base timeouts (same definition as arm 1).
    91	- SAFETY: test-file edits 0 rows; stray files 0 rows; total wall p90 <= 1.10 x the base arm's total wall p90; empty-patch rows
    92	  <= base + 3; submitted-without-any-test-run <= base + 3 (plan 008 definition and regex).
    93	- DESCRIPTIVE: root thinking blocks per task (count, total chars, tasks with > 0); context-overflow rows; repeat metric (plan 008
    94	  MECHANISM 2 definition: tasks with max identical run >= 5, max run, total repeated); LLM calls and tool calls p50/p90; per repo;
    95	  the 25 never-screened ids separately.
